Red signal: batch 22 review, item-review-batch-22.json (kimi-code-plan-cn/kimi-for-coding). The
green door passed at 8.0, the low table passed at 7.5, the Pat page v2 failed at 5.0. Critical
defect: "Pat's face is not visible. The page shows the back of his head, so a child cannot see who
Pat is on the page that introduces him."

Step A, the animal pictures. Cause is in the asset geometry. The frame was a 0.014 m box at z 0 to
0.014 and the picture backdrop ran from z 0.004 to 0.024, so the picture face sat 0.010 m in front
of the frame front. At the oblique classroom camera the border read as a second board offset behind
the picture, with the frame's bottom side face as the wood tab below each picture. Fix: the frame is
now a border ring of the full picture depth, FRAME_DEPTH 0.038 m (flush with the front face of the
deepest animal layer), cut from a 0.55 by 0.45 m box with a 0.49 by 0.39 m opening; the backdrop is
0.01 m wider than the opening so its edge sits inside the frame.
Asset renders: first render exit 0 but the back plate of 0.004 m is thinner than the 0.007 m mesh
cell and collapsed, so the picture colors showed through from behind. FRAME_BACK rose to 0.012 m.
Second render exit 0, `./forge inspect storytime-animal-pictures --fast` exit 0 with the same two
notes as round 49 only (lion-nose barely visible; side silhouette very thin). No `warning:` line.
Logs: green-p3-r51-asset.log, green-p3-r51-asset2.log.

